<title>USA: Ford looking to create superstores - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Ford looking to create superstores - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ford Motor Co is considering joining with dealers in three U.S. cities to create auto superstores, the Wall Street Journal said in Monday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>The venture would allow Ford, which now solely manufactures cars and trucks, to sell their vehicles directly to customers.</p>
<p>Ford said it is considering the venture with Ford and Lincoln-Mercury dealers in Indianapolis, and then naming two other cities at a later date.</p>
<p>The company said it would not force dealers to participate in a venture it hopes will compete against auto-retail chains.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
